# What .env.local (git-ignored) holds: the settings of this clone's deployment, which every script reads through
# scripts\Use-IsolatedAzure.ps1. There's no need to copy this file: the Config step of scripts\Deploy-AdvisorTeam.ps1
# writes .env.local from its parameters, and later steps add what they create (listed at the end). To change a
# setting, edit .env.local, or rerun the Config step with -Force to rewrite it from the parameters.

# Written by the Config step. The isolated profile (sign-ins, Terraform state, the Python environment and work files)
# lives under %LOCALAPPDATA%\advisor-team\<TEAM_PROFILE>. From -ProfileName, -TenantId, -SubscriptionId and
# -NameSuffix (the suffix of this deployment's tenant-wide names; default: the profile name).
TEAM_PROFILE=demo
AZURE_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
TEAM_NAME_SUFFIX=demo

# Shared resources to reuse under new names (logical isolation; see docs/ISOLATION.md), from -ExistingFoundryAccountId,
# -ExistingFabricCapacityId and -ExistingSearchServiceId. Empty: everything is created from scratch. The safety checks
# for shared resources read them from here, and later runs of the deploy script can leave the parameters out.
EXISTING_FOUNDRY_ACCOUNT_ID=
EXISTING_FABRIC_CAPACITY_ID=
EXISTING_SEARCH_SERVICE_ID=

# The story's people, from -AnalystUpn and -ClientEmail; the names are the signed-in admin's (or -AdvisorName) and the
# analyst's display names.
DEMO_ADVISOR_NAME=
DEMO_ANALYST_NAME=
DEMO_ANALYST_UPN=
DEMO_CLIENT_EMAIL=michael.scott@scott-family.example

# The story's week: its client meeting, a Thursday (yyyy-MM-dd; from -StoryMeetingDate, default the next Thursday). It
# moves the hydrated story's dates (data/hydration, evals). To rehearse an existing story before its dates, give the
# agent a clock floor in terraform.tfvars instead:
#   agent_extra_environment = { ADVISOR_CLOCK_NOT_BEFORE = "2026-10-20T13:00:00Z" }
STORY_MEETING_DATE=

# Optional, set by hand; some scripts read them:
#   WEB_BOUNDARY_TERMS       names (comma-separated) the rehearsal checks never reach the market agent; an agent run
#                            locally also keeps them out of Web IQ. The hosted agent gets its own list (the story's
#                            clients, the advisor and the analyst) from terraform\terraform.tfvars
#   DEMO_ADVISOR_UPN         the account scripts\accept_consent.py uses
#   TEAM_PROJECT_ENDPOINT    the Foundry project endpoint for scripts\rehearse.py and scripts\review_packs.py
#                            (default: the Terraform output, which needs this machine's Terraform state)
#   FABRIC_WORKSPACE_NAME    the Fabric workspace's name (default: Advisor Team)
#   ADVISOR_CANDIDATE_AGENT  the quality loop's candidate agent (default: <agent>-candidate)
#   DRAFT_MODE               the review packs' drafts when the agent runs locally (default: preview, shown, never saved)

# Recorded by the deployment steps; don't set these by hand:
#   the Fabric step      FABRIC_WORKSPACE_ID, FABRIC_LAKEHOUSE_ID, FABRIC_SQL_ENDPOINT, FABRIC_CAPACITY_NAME,
#                        FABRIC_CAPACITY_ID, FABRIC_DATA_AGENT_ID, FABRIC_DATA_AGENT_MCP_URL, FABRIC_IQ_CONNECTION_ID,
#                        FABRIC_IQ_CONNECTION_NAME
#   the FoundryIq step   FOUNDRY_IQ_MCP_URL, FOUNDRY_IQ_CONNECTION_ID, FOUNDRY_IQ_KB_NAME
#   the WebIq step       WEBIQ_CONNECTION_NAME
#   evals\Invoke-AdvisorEval.ps1   ADVISOR_EVAL_ID
# The region, the resource group and the specialist region aren't kept here: they are the deploy script's -Location,
# -ResourceGroup and -SpecialistLocation, written to terraform\terraform.tfvars.
